  "abstract": "Constructs a discrete AQUAL-like gravity operator on a cubic graph with entropic flux weighting that reproduces Newtonian (g \u221d r\u207b\u00b2) and MOND-like (g \u221d r\u207b\u00b9) regimes without assuming a continuum metric. A \u039b-locked bulk entropic reservoir sets the transition scale (L_\u039b \u221d \u039b\u207b\u00b9\u141f\u00b2), yielding a convergent deep-MOND prefactor C \u2248 2.32 (implying a0,eff \u2248 5.4 a0), broken superposition, an external field effect, and a weak mass-scaling exponent r_trans \u221d M^0.18. A minimal cosmological stability check shows ~0.7\u20130.8% suppression in \u03c38/f\u03c38 via background-only modification.",
